// APW-5 -- Session splitting (BUGGY): "at most 3 sends per session".
//
// The *intent* is a per-session cap.  The *bug* is in the runtime counter:
// the session counter is reset to 1 after every send, so the guard
// (`scope_count < 3`) is always satisfied and N sessions each admit 3 sends --
// the total is N x the per-session cap.  The Classmethod tutorial itself notes
// that temporal limits are per-session; this shape makes the split explicit.
//
// This is a *concept* sample: Dogwood has no per-session scoping operator yet,
// so this does not lower to a ROTN shape.  The hand-written oracle
// (rot.shapes.build_scoped_cap_ir) models the broken counter and is what ROTN
// decides: VIOLATED, witness session_count=4, scope_count=1.
//
// See: docs/apw-catalog.md (APW-5), tests/test_apw5.py.

@id("apw5_buggy")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Send",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum 1 for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Send"::request{} && tp(t))
    )) > 3
};
